Write $p(T)=\sum_k c_kT^k$. Then $p(XY)=\sum_k c_kX^kY^k$. Distinct monomials preserve the coefficients, so a nonzero $p$ produces a nonzero bivariate polynomial. If $p(xy)=0$, that polynomial vanishes at $(x,y)$, contradicting algebraic independence.

</details>

